      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables name and value\n    price_changes = [\n        1.2, -0.8, 0.5, 2.3, -1.0, -0.4, 1.8,\n        0.6, -1.5, 3.0, -0.2, -0.9, 2.1, 0.7\n    ]\n    period = 14\n\n    # Do math calculation to get the answer\n    gains = [max(change, 0) for change in price_changes]\n    losses = [abs(min(change, 0)) for change in price_changes]\n\n    average_gain = sum(gains[:period]) / period\n    average_loss = sum(losses[:period]) / period\n\n    if average_loss == 0:\n        rsi = 100.0\n    else:\n        relative_strength = average_gain / average_loss\n        rsi = 100 - (100 / (1 + relative_strength))\n\n    # Return the RSI as a percentage rounded to two decimal places\n    return round(rsi, 2)\n```",
